    12	## What is registered
    13	
    14	- **Parameters** (A9.2; frozen profile §1): δ = 72 h, ε = 24 h, k = 6, N = 3, S = 24 h.
    15	- **Attempts** (A2.3, `:259-268`): at most N. Each has its own declared issue time. A retry that changes any
    16	  committed byte needs a fresh stamp (A9.5, `phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md:295`), and its signatures are frozen
    17	  before it is stamped (A9.5, `:290-296`).
    18	- **Eligibility** (A2.1 `:91-94`; A2.2 `:220-224`; A3.7.3 `:659-673`): the attempt's own authenticated evidence for
    19	  `SHA256(A_sig)`, with the lowest qualifying height buried k = 6 deep on the pinned, linked segment (profile §7.1),
    20	  satisfies all three conjuncts: `declared − ε ≤ T`, `T ≤ declared + δ`, and `confirmed_at ≤ declared + δ`. This
    21	  is narrower than the whole `VALID_STRICT` verdict, and the remaining pre-ship checks stay separate. Rows 12.2 and
    22	  12.3 of the verifier are two of the conjuncts, not the predicate.
    23	- **Latch and expiry** (A2.1 `:150-162`): eligibility observed at or before `B = declared + δ + S` is timely. The
    24	  boundary is inclusive and "latch-winning", and a latched attempt cannot expire. Expiry applies only strictly
    25	  after B, and only to attempts with no timely-latched eligibility. Atomicity of latch against expiry is an
    26	  obligation on the implementation (A2.3). If the predicate fails at issuance time, the attempt is discarded and
    27	  re-issued, subject to N (A2.1 `:161-162`). A lag beyond S *may* be refused (A2.1 `:135-138`); refusing it is not
    28	  required.
    29	- **Refusal** (A2.3 `:265-268, :279-281`): exhausting N ends issuance in an explicit refusal, durably recorded, and
    30	  the transition that expires the final attempt records the refusal in the same step. In V1 the refusal is local and
    31	  returned by the API (A9.7 row 12; `docs/V1-CLARIFICATIONS.md` CL-03). A3's portable record, commitment and
    32	  publication are not V1.
    33	- **Budget** (A2.3 `:271-274, :288-289`): N × (δ + S), twelve days, is a *nominal* budget, "not a proven wall-clock
    34	  bound". Termination is an obligation on the implementation, not a proven liveness property.
    35	- **Window** (A9 `:422`): an attempt whose T would exceed not-after is not shipped.
    36	- **No SLA here** (A2.1 `:139-142`): a hard latency bound may enter only as a deployment-profile item with monitoring
    37	  and an explicit violation outcome. It never kills an eligible attempt.
    38	
    39	## What the issuer does
    40	
    41	1. **Attempt isolation.** A request holds attempts 1..N. Each attempt has its own id. Its declared time, frames,
    42	   signature jobs, proofs and evidence live under that id, in object names and record fields. A signer response, a
    43	   proof or a frame always names its attempt. A late response for attempt i is logged and ignored. It can never fill
    44	   attempt j.
    45	2. **Eligibility check** (any poll, any worker): fetch or upgrade the attempt's evidence, then evaluate the
    46	   eligibility predicate above, with the observation instant taken as a wall reading *after* the evidence is in hand.
    47	   If it holds, **latch**: a compare-and-set write of `latched_at` together with the evidence digests. Latching
    48	   needs no margin, because the latch is not raced. See step 3.
    49	3. **Expiry is decided only by re-observation.** A worker may expire attempt i only if, in the same decision:
    50	   - (a) it read the record and found i not latched;
    51	   - (b) it took a wall reading strictly after B, after the read;
    52	   - (c) it fetched the chain evidence itself and found the predicate false (or a conjunct permanently failed).
    53	
    54	   The expiry write is compare-and-set on the version it read. So a timely eligibility can never be lost to a stale
    55	   expirer: the expirer recomputes the chain facts it would be overriding, and a concurrent latch makes its write
    56	   fail. If the evidence cannot be fetched (calendar or explorer outage), the attempt is not expired on that poll.
    57	   A request whose evidence stays unobtainable is refused only by the rule in step 6. This uses the permitted choice
    58	   of A2.1: chain-eligible evidence observed after B, while the attempt is still open, is accepted. An attempt that
    59	   has expired is never reopened.
    60	4. **Known-invalid evidence.** If a conjunct has failed permanently (for example, the lowest qualifying height is
    61	   later than `declared + δ` with k-deep burial), the attempt is discarded at once and the next one starts. It does
    62	   not wait for B (A2.1 `:161-162`).
    63	5. **Retry.** After an expiry or discard, if fewer than N attempts have been made and signing is open (signing stop,
    64	   `sign_by`), attempt i+1 starts with a fresh declared time, fresh frames, fresh signatures and a fresh stamp. A
    65	   closed signing window prevents *new* signatures only. It never expires a latched attempt, or an attempt already
    66	   signed and stamped that can still become eligible.
    67	6. **Refusal.** When the last attempt expires or is discarded, or no further attempt can start, the same
    68	   compare-and-set write sets the request to REFUSED with its reason: `ATTEMPTS_EXHAUSTED`, `SIGNING_CLOSED` or
    69	   `EVIDENCE_UNAVAILABLE`. That reason is used when evidence has been unobtainable for a stated operating period
    70	   after B (an operating number, recorded in the runbook). The refusal is terminal and durable, returned by the API,
    71	   and kept under S5.
    72	7. **After the latch.** A latched attempt proceeds to assembly and the pre-ship checks. A *transient* failure (an
    73	   explorer, a calendar, a DNS snapshot, a store) is retried and never expires the attempt. A *permanent* pre-ship
    74	   failure of a latched attempt (for example T > not-after, or a verifier verdict other than `VALID_STRICT` for a
    75	   reason the attempt cannot cure) discards that attempt with a recorded reason, and step 5 applies. An attempt
    76	   that cannot be shipped is not shipped, and "every timely-eligible attempt ships" is honoured as far as the
    77	   window invariant allows.
    78	8. **Public view.** `fail_after` is withdrawn. The status shows `state`, `attempt` (i of N), and for an open,
    79	   unlatched attempt its `attempt_expires_after` = B. It says plainly that a later attempt may follow, and that the
    80	   twelve days are a nominal budget, not a promise.
    81	9. **Clock tolerance.** The CF2-01 lease margin no longer applies to completion: COMPLETE follows a latch, and the
    82	   latch is not raced. The 15-minute tolerance still bounds visibility of the other transitions
    83	   (`docs/decisions/2026-10-27-service-clock-tolerance.md`). It never shrinks B.
