Step 3 still permits a race: a worker can observe eligibility before B, while an expirer fetches older or partial evidence and wins the compare-and-set before the latch write. CAS prevents two writes from winning on one version; it does not ensure the timely observation wins. I’m also checking whether the new refusal rule can terminate an attempt whose timely eligibility remains unknown to that worker.
